.po 1i
.TH FOREACH 1C UCB
.V 08/15/84 16:51:49
.\"@[$]foreach.1C	1.6	08/15/84 16:51:49 - Zilog Inc.
.ad
.SH NAME
foreach \- C Shell flow control loop initiation
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B foreach
.I name 
.I "( list )"
.in +5m
.I command
.in -5m
.B end
.SH DESCRIPTION
The variable
.I name
is successively set to each member of
.I wordlist
and the sequence of commands between this command and the matching
.B end
are executed.
Both
.B foreach
and
.B end
must appear alone on separate lines.
.PP
When this command is read from the terminal, the loop is read up once
prompting with ? before any statements in the loop are executed.
A typing mistake in a loop at the terminal can be rubbed out.
.SH FILES
/bin/csh
.SH SEE ALSO
break(1C),
breaksw(1C), 
continue(1C),
exit(1C),
if(1C),
nohup(1C),
onintr(1C),
switch(1C),
while(1C).
.br
\fIThe C Shell\fR in the ZEUS Utilities Manual
